--- body ---
## Context

Bug hunt on the `erg archive` / `erg close` move path. `cmdArchive`'s mover
(`MkdirAll closed/` + `os.Stat` collision check + `os.Rename`, archive.go:146-164)
is the primitive 0248 extracts into a shared `moveTicketToClosed` helper and
routes `erg close` through. These defects exist in `archive` today and 0248
would make every `close` inherit them, so the hardening must land in the shared
helper.

## Findings (reproduced against a scratch store in /tmp)

- **[blocker] Symlinked `closed/` silently exfiltrates the ticket out of the
  store.** archive.go:146-164. If `tickets/closed` is a symlink to an out-of-store
  dir, `MkdirAll` is a no-op and `os.Rename` follows the symlinked parent
  component, moving the `.erg` OUTSIDE the store; `erg check` then reports
  "no files / PASS". The mover never calls `withinStore`, the only confinement
  rail in the code — and atomicwrite.go's "symlink AT the target is harmless"
  reasoning does not cover a symlink as a parent dir component, which is exactly
  what `closed/` is. Direct "never lose data" violation; 0248 makes every `close`
  inherit it. Repro: `ln -s /tmp/escape store/tickets/closed; erg archive
  store/tickets` -> ticket lands in /tmp/escape, check PASS.
  Fix: in `moveTicketToClosed`, `filepath.EvalSymlinks` the `closed` parent (or
  `os.Lstat` and refuse a symlinked `closed`) and re-assert `withinStore(ticketDir,
  dst)` before `os.Rename`.

- **[major] Destination-collision returns exit 0 but leaves a permanent
  check-failing wedge.** archive.go:155-158. On `os.Stat(dst) == nil` archive
  prints "destination already exists, skipping" and `continue`s with exitCode
  unchanged (0). The source stays top-level; `erg check` then HARD-FAILS
  ("closed ticket not in closed/ -- run 'erg archive'") and re-running archive
  just re-skips forever (exit 0 each time). A scripted caller / the pre-push hook
  sees success while the corpus is permanently broken. Realistic trigger: two
  slugs sharing one ID (one archived, one hand-closed top-level) -> identical
  `closed/<ID>-slug.erg` basename. 0248 makes `close` hit this too (the
  fall-through-to-move for closed-but-top-level), so close becomes silently
  corpus-breaking. Fix: on collision the shared helper returns a non-nil error
  (exit 1); optionally treat a same-content collision as a no-op success.

- **[minor] `closed/` existing as a regular FILE aborts the move with the header
  already committed.** archive.go:146-150. `MkdirAll` fails "not a directory",
  exit 1, ticket stranded top-level. Benign for standalone archive, but under
  0248 the `Closed:` header + log are already fsync-written before the move, so
  the failed move leaves a committed-closed ticket that `erg check` flags. Fix:
  helper returns a clear error; `close` reports the partial state.

- **[minor] Dry-run diverges from the real run on collision.** archive.go:139-143
  (`-n` prints "WOULD ARCHIVE") vs 154-158 (real prints "skipping"). The pre-push
  hook relies on `archive -n` as a truthful preview; here it over-promises. Fix:
  replicate the `os.Stat(dst)` check in the dry-run branch ("WOULD SKIP").

## Test

- Symlinked `closed/`: `erg archive`/`erg close` must REFUSE (or keep the ticket
  in-store), never relocate outside; `erg check` stays meaningful.
- Collision: archiving onto an existing `closed/<ID>-slug.erg` exits non-zero and
  leaves a clear error, not a silent exit-0 wedge.
- `closed/` as a file: clear error, reported partial state.
- Dry-run matches the real run on a colliding ticket.

## Exit criteria

The shared `moveTicketToClosed` helper re-asserts in-store confinement after
symlink resolution and never relocates a ticket outside the store; destination
collisions and a non-dir `closed/` surface as non-zero errors, not exit-0 wedges;
dry-run previews collisions; `erg archive` keeps its current happy-path behavior;
`make check` and `make verify` pass.
